     <div class="meta">Health Promotion and Maintenance · Multiple choice · Recognize cues</div>
     <h1 class="stem">A laboring client is 8 cm dilated, irritable, nauseated, and says she can't go on. Which phase of labor is she in?</h1><ol><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-hpm3-013"> <span><b>A.</b> Latent phase of the first stage</span></label></li><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-hpm3-013"> <span><b>B.</b> Second stage</span></label></li><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-hpm3-013"> <span><b>C.</b> Third stage</span></label></li><li data-c="1"><label><input type="radio" name="q-hpm3-013"> <span><b>D.</b> Transition phase of the first stage</span></label></li></ol>
     <button class="btn chk" type="button">Check answer</button><p class="res" aria-live="polite"></p>
     <details><summary>Show answer and rationale</summary><p class="ans">Correct answer: D</p><p>Transition is the end of active first stage labor (about 8 to 10 cm). Intense contractions, irritability, nausea, and feeling out of control are common.</p><p class="src">Source: Lowdermilk. Maternity &amp; Women's Health Care, 13th ed. (stages of labor)</p></details>
     </article>
      <div class="share"><button data-share type="button">Share this question</button><a href="/question-of-the-day">Question of the day</a></div>
      <h2>Keep practicing Health Promotion and Maintenance</h2><p>This question is one of 129 Health Promotion and Maintenance items in Vexcura. On the NCLEX-RN, this category makes up 6–12% of the exam.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/#practice/HPM">Practice more Health Promotion and Maintenance questions</a><a class="btn alt" href="/free-nclex-practice-exam">Take the full practice exam</a></div>
      <div class="tips"><b>Study tip</b><ul><li>Build a one-page growth and development grid by age: gross motor, fine motor, language, play, and safety teaching.</li><li>Review prenatal landmarks (fundal height, Naegele's rule, danger signs) and postpartum assessment (BUBBLE-HE).</li></ul></div>
      <h3>More free Health Promotion and Maintenance questions</h3><ul><li><a href="/nclex-questions/contraceptive-method-also-helps-protect-against-sexually-hpm3-018">Which contraceptive method also helps protect against sexually transmitted infections?</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-questions/sunscreen-guidance-give-hpm3-019">Which sunscreen guidance should the nurse give?</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-questions/pregnant-asks-she-feel-baby-move-say-hpm3-009">A pregnant client asks when she will first feel the baby move. What should the nurse say?</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-questions/signs-show-infant-developmentally-ready-start-solid-hpm4-020">Which signs show that an infant is developmentally ready to start solid foods? Select all that apply.</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-questions/finding-indicates-true-labor-rather-false-labor-hpm3-012">Which finding indicates true labor rather than false labor?</a></li></ul>
